    },
    {
      "text": "The 5.00 SGD charged is exactly the no-show fee POL-NS-22 sets, and the payments ledger reconciles to that single cancellation-fee line with no other charge, so no POL-NS-22 fee-amount referral arises on this record. Had the fee stood it would have been payable to the driver as compensation for time and fuel at 1.00 fee share.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-FARE-05052].payload.derived.money.fee_charged_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-NS-24 goodwill credit is due to the rider. That credit requires both that the driver failed to arrive at the pickup in time AND that the driver also failed to attempt contact, and the driver plainly did attempt contact: two in-app messages were sent at 19:31:30 and 19:34:10, both delivered and both read by the rider before the cancellation. The second limb therefore fails and the additional 5.00 SGD credit cannot attach.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05052", "EV-TRIP-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-CHAT-05052].payload.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's stated reason for missing the driver — that she was 'in the lift with no signal' — is not borne out by the record: the chat log shows she read the driver's first message at 19:31:40 and his second at 19:34:23, both before the 19:37:20 cancellation, so in-app traffic was reaching her throughout the wait. Her account of being unreachable is therefore not reliable, and she simply did not come to the pickup while the driver waited there.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-CHAT-05052].payload.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I concede the decisive point on the money, and I do not stretch the record to avoid it. POL-NS-23 requires the driver, before cancelling for no-show, both to have sent at least one in-app message AND to have placed at least one in-app call, evidenced by trip_record.in_app_calls or a voice-call entry in the chat log. The trip record's in_app_calls is empty and the chat log contains only text entries — messages MSG-05052-001 and MSG-05052-002 — with no voice-call entry, and both artifacts are COMPLETE with no admissibility issue. The call limb of the contact obligation is therefore not met on this record, and on POL-NS-23's terms the fee falls to be voided in full. The driver's compliance with arrival and free wait does not cure that defect, and no POL-NS-23 argument is available to me.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052", "EV-CHAT-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-TRIP-05052].payload.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
