    "explanation": "Dear Rider and Driver, this dispute turns on the driver's contact obligation before cancelling, and it is decided on that clause alone.\n\nUnder POL-NS-23, before cancelling a trip as a rider no-show the driver must BOTH send at least one in-app chat message AND place at least one in-app call to the rider, both before the cancellation. The message limb is met: the chat log (EV-CHAT-05052, complete, weight 1.0) shows two driver messages, MSG-05052-001 at 19:31:30 and MSG-05052-002 at 19:34:10. The call limb is not met: the trip record (EV-TRIP-05052, complete, weight 1.0) carries an empty in_app_calls array, and the chat log contains no voice-call entry. The derived contact test on the trip record itself returns obligation_met = false with call_count 0. Failing either limb voids the fee, so the 5.00 SGD charged at 19:37:24 (EV-FARE-05052: total_charged 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, refund_if_voided_sgd 5.00) is returned in full to the rider and no compensation is payable to the driver.\n\nDriver advocate's points: the arrival at 19:31:00 marked on the trip record is corroborated by the GPS trace (EV-GPS-05052, nearest fix 2.73 m from the pickup with 5 m reported accuracy, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and the 25 m filter), and the 300 s free wait under POL-NS-21 did run before the 19:37:20 cancellation (380 s from arrival). I accept both facts, but they cannot cure the missing call, which independently voids the fee under POL-NS-23. The 5.00 SGD charged is exactly POL-NS-22's no-show fee, so no fee-amount referral arises. I also accept that no POL-NS-24 goodwill credit attaches: that credit needs both a missed arrival deadline and a failure to attempt contact, and the driver did attempt contact with two delivered and read messages, so the second limb fails. The rider's read receipts do undercut her account of being out of signal, but that point decides nothing here.\n\nRider advocate's points: the missing call (accepted, decisive); the consequence is FULL_REFUND of the fee charged (accepted, 5.00 SGD); no driver compensation follows a voided fee (accepted, driver_compensation is null); the driver's own statement asserts no call and is consistent with the record (accepted); the refund does not depend on the rider answering the messages (accepted); and the absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05052-01 (status MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and is not needed by any no-show clause (accepted, it plays no part in this ruling).\n\nNo escalation applies. The deciding facts are carried by artifacts complete at weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-05052 and EV-CHAT-05052), the contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither party carries a fraud flag, so under POL-NS-26 the AI ruling on this no-show is final. No clause produces a referral: the fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD POL-NS-22 sets, no goodwill credit is due under POL-NS-24, and the POL-NS-25 repeat no-show counter is not present on the rider profile and the fee does not stand in any event."
